%% mmdc -i public/images/authentication/openid-backchannel-logout.mmd -o public/images/authentication/openid-backchannel-logout.svg -b white
sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: OpenID back-channel logout
    accDescr: Login binds credentials to the provider session. A signed logout notification revokes that session. Existing access tokens remain valid until expiry. The next restoration or renewal is denied and the browser signs out.
    participant B as Browser
    participant P as OpenID provider
    participant L as LibreChat
    participant D as Session records
    Note over B,D: record or enforce mode
    B->>P: Sign in
    P-->>L: Verified login with sid
    L->>D: Link credentials to<br/>the provider session
    L-->>B: Issue credentials
    P->>L: POST signed logout_token
    L->>L: Validate signature<br/>and claims
    L->>D: Mark matching<br/>session revoked
    L-->>P: 200 OK
    Note over B,D: Existing access token remains valid until expiry
    B->>L: Restore or renew session
    L->>D: Check linked<br/>provider session
    D-->>L: Revoked
    L-->>B: 401 OPENID_SESSION_ENDED
    B->>B: Sign out
